diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 6460f87..2b412fc 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,3 +1,78 @@
+#### 2.0.7-quality.16
+
+* Remove Appearance, Inbound, DNS and Presets from Settings, including their editors.
+* Follow the system light and dark mode with the built-in theme and keep existing VPN profiles and connection settings.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.15
+
+* Remove the home-screen status and toggle widgets and their background updates.
+* Remove unused helpers and translations for features removed in earlier builds.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.14
+
+* Remove the bundled sing-box dashboard, its WebView startup code and the real-time graphs and sampling pipeline.
+* Remove the About screen, its UI dependency and the obsolete whole-group actions. Keep the bundled license.
+* Retain the sing-box API, traffic counters, speed tests and subscription filters.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.13
+
+* Start the TPROXY root process while the main core prepares the connection.
+* Install private firewall chains in batches on devices that support it, with the original rule-by-rule fallback.
+* Report connection startup timings in the log.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.12
+
+* Simplify the profiles toolbar, overflow menu, drawer and settings to match the marked screenshots.
+* Keep profile imports and editors, connection tests, route data, the VPN core and backup flows.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.11
+
+* Let Android VPN routes reach their VPN interface directly in TPROXY mode so they use the Android VPN's exit IP.
+* Update IPv4 and IPv6 interception when the VPN interface changes, honoring Android's split-tunnel policy.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.10
+
+* Report the local TPROXY relay's loopback interface to the core at startup.
+* Reject intercepted QUIC promptly with TCP-only Naive to allow TCP fallback, preserving alternate UDP routes.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.9
+
+* Exclude Android VPN clients from TPROXY before they connect, including their initial DNS and server connections.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.7
+
+* Route TPROXY's upstream traffic and system DNS through the Android VPN when it covers Throne.
+* Keep the VPN's protected transport sockets out of TPROXY and reconnect upstream sessions when the VPN changes.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.6
+
+* Stop the TPROXY core and release its routes when switching or closing the service.
+* Skip reply packets in the transparent interception chain and report TCP and UDP counts in the journal.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.5
+
+* Put the root TPROXY core cache in the app cache directory so it can start.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.4
+
+* Show TPROXY (root) in the localized service mode menu.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.3
+
+* Run TPROXY on Android 14 or later using the special-use foreground service type.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.2
+
+* Add a TPROXY (root) service mode for device TCP and UDP on IPv4 and IPv6.
+* Require root and kernel TPROXY support. Restore the session's firewall chains and policy routes when it stops.
+
+#### 2.0.7-quality.1
+
+* Add a sequential connection quality test for the current group.
+* Show the saved score from 1 to 100 in red on each profile card.
+* Score HTTPS availability and response times, WebSocket echo, and SSE delivery.
+* Use a separate Android package so the build can be installed alongside upstream Throne.
+
 #### 2.0.7
 
 * Add Service check **1**
